W1700K firmware customizations

The GitHub upgrade UI and helper are new implementations by
openwrt-w1700k-builds contributors (2026), licensed GPL-2.0-only.
The release selection feature was inspired by w1700k/builds.

The six diagnostic scripts in root/etc are imported from:
https://github.com/w1700k/builds/tree/9449e4ca242ab30278df20940d6654ddc1c102e8/user/default/files/etc
They retain that repository's GPL-2.0-only license. There were no individual
copyright notices in these files; existing comments and script logic are
preserved. Local changes on 2026-09-18 add executable interpreter lines,
normalize whitespace, and require an explicit opt-in to testgpio.sh.
They are never run automatically.

The single-wiphy change is a new Apache-2.0 implementation for luci-mod-status.
LuCI copyright: The LuCI Team and contributors. Its existing notices remain
unchanged. The problem and earlier workaround are credited to Gilly1970
in w1700k/builds' 998-single-wiphy.patch and to the reporters of:
https://github.com/openwrt/luci/issues/7483
The earlier patch text was not copied because its independent license grant
was not explicit. The new patch is an exception to this builder's GPL-2.0-only
default and retains the target component's Apache-2.0 licensing.

The missing-wireless-device fix in luci-base is a new Apache-2.0 change
by ACK72 (2026), retaining the target LuCI component's license.

The low-rate npu-jitter-daemon replacement, first-boot enable script, and
FlowSense mean-RTT presentation patch are new Apache-2.0 changes by ACK72
(2026). FlowSense's existing Apache-2.0 notices remain unchanged.

The version-guarded mwan3 route-state installer is an Apache-2.0 change by
ACK72 (2026). It moves an existing call in the user's separately installed
mwan3 3.6.12 source; the upstream mwan3 license is not changed.

The netdev-add packet-steering hook follows the narrowly scoped suggestion in
Gilly1970/Gemtek-W1700K-6.18 at f72939518d0bd3f02c26f42a4d08c4452cb48a9f.
It does not import that tree's PCIe IRQ-affinity or packet-steering policy.

